# E3  B alone: spin-1/2 per link end, two per cell, distinguishable.
#     Alternating ring: J_link = +1 (AF) across links, J_cell inside a cell.
#     J_cell -> -inf is the spin-1 chain (gap -> 0.4105/4 = 0.103);
#     J_cell = 0 is isolated link singlets (gap 1); J_cell = +1 is the
#     uniform spin-1/2 chain (gapless).  The gap moves continuously.
  J_cell   gap(4 cells)  gap(6 cells)  gap(8 cells)
   +1.0       0.5227       0.3558       0.2702
   +0.5       0.6817       0.6608       0.6579
   +0.0       1.0000       1.0000       1.0000
   -0.5       0.7819       0.7808       0.7807
   -1.0       0.6274       0.6191       0.6183
   -2.0       0.4581       0.4273       0.4207
   -4.0       0.3440       0.2893       0.2708
   -8.0       0.2908       0.2258       0.1994
E3 verdict: with the on-site rule left free, B's gap (and so xi) is a
   continuous function of J_cell/J_link. A's bosonic modes fix J_cell = -inf.
